  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In this figure the resistance of the coil of galvanometer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>. The emf of the cell is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The ratio of potential difference across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6d9686e7-80ba-46b9-bbe3-b2be870ab6c6.png\" style=\"width: 340px; height: 278px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
